  "validation_sequence": [
    "All listed native cases and eight CTest groups ran on the final production binaries and depth helper, including the bounded traversal-stack refinement.",
    "After the full native runs, only the generation fixture was corrected: one-line shader directives had failed to register hint/skip flags. The earlier full-run generation_guard object is superseded by the separate corrected_generation_guard result.",
    "The final multiline hint/skip fixture and 1061-face assertion passed with --generation-only on all three unchanged production binaries. Each run rejects 1025 explicit hint planes and preserves previous BSP/SRF bytes.",
    "Final core executables were also run directly on all three platforms to bind the 1400/809 oracle counts to fresh logs."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Automatic block boundary sets and axis priority remain; cut order and node/plane/leaf IDs may change. This is not general byte compatibility or automatic regional VIS merging.",
    "Generated axial fixtures establish exact cell geometry, rendered triangle XYZ/ST/normals and mapped PVS equivalence where reference comparisons are enabled. They do not prove arbitrary-map or engine-rendering equivalence.",
    "Windows and Linux use preceding-compiler reference comparisons. Sanitizer native cases use independent expected geometry, clear sightlines and guard outcomes without a reference compiler.",
    "Reader graph fixtures are synthetic node graphs; their at-limit acceptance is not a claim of geometrically meaningful BSP geometry.",
    "The graph helper checks every component and longest path; the generation fixture exercises rejection before publication. No separate native writer-only corruption injection was used.",
    "The 1024-node limit bounds BSP path depth and traversal frames, not all compiler resources or every recursive algorithm. State and height arrays remain proportional to node count.",
    "Previous BSP/SRF bytes survive the generation-depth failure. Existing startup PRT/LIN/REG cleanup remains outside this guarantee.",
    "ASan/UBSan run with the established leak-detection exclusion. The existing vis_reproducible sanitizer fixture uses grid 5 instead of the release grid 9.",
    "No game, user-input control, OS screenshot, peak-memory measurement or compile-speed benchmark was used for this round."
  ]
